    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GJKDpNGp4ZJfeMjMdUzpoQ)_\n\n## What\nAfter #155, clicking a `help:` link raised `Wrong type argument: stringp, nil`.\n\nCause, from the backtrace: `describe-function` mentions the shortdoc groups of a function, which loads `shortdoc`. `taxy` has registered its group with a nil section name, so `shortdoc-add-function` fails as soon as `shortdoc` loads. `C-h f` on the same function fails the same way, so it is not specific to the links.\n\n- `sp-help`: advice on `shortdoc-add-function` turns a nil section into an empty string. Remove it once `taxy` is fixed.\n- `sp-org-id-link`: `help:` also gets its own follow function (`sp-org-link-follow-help`) that opens faces, which the completer offers and Org's follow function rejects.\n- Docs and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). The advice is based on the backtrace you sent.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAJc2Qd7A97uwG84ky)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAJc2Qd7A97uwG84ky",
